<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZCC to rule on Goodman by April 14.</title>
<headline>NZCC to rule on Goodman by April 14.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Commerce Commission said on Wednesday its decision on Goodman Fielder Ltd's application for clearance to buy the New Zealand baking and milling assets of Defiance Mills Ltd would be made by 5.00 p.m. on April 14.</p>
<p>The Commission said it was to have released its decision on Thursday, but wanted more time to consider all the relevant issues.</p>
<p>New Zealand's Commerce Act prohibits business acquisitions that result in dominance being acquired or strengthened in any market.  </p>
<p>--Wellington Newsroom (64 4) 4734746</p>
</text>
